From d82d825e461e89a5c9e6dd25b1012491c3c35b9b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 03:50:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Run the map path in fp32 and fail fast on non-finite weights
 or activations

R7 (student initialised from the LLM-grid pretraining step 460000 with
load_pretrained_map_modules=True) died in its first DAgger iteration with NaN
action probabilities on every environment. The pretrained map encoder and
fusion had never run inside the trainer before: pretraining runs them in fp32,
the DAgger rollout runs under fp16 autocast, and the earlier runs only ever
saw these modules at their (small) initial weights.

- EmbeddingGridMapEncoder and both map-fusion modules now disable autocast and
  compute in fp32, matching the precision they were pretrained in.
- nan_guard.assert_finite_parameters runs once after weights are loaded and
  names any non-finite tensor (student and teacher).
- nan_guard.NonFiniteOutputGuard hooks every submodule of the student policy
  and, after each root forward, raises naming the first module whose output
  held NaN/+inf (-inf is allowed: masks use it). Enabled by ETP_NAN_DEBUG_STEPS,
  which the distillation launchers default to 1000 forwards; the hooks remove
  themselves afterwards. launch_info.txt records the setting.
- Tests cover the guard semantics and the fp32 fusion output under autocast.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Xm3S8jGTjU1YqXnUPuWMgH
